WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.689
Caroline pedaled up the driveway, looking for a spot to park her bike.

2
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:20.934
Her usual spot was occupied by junk Dad had found at a flea market—tools, flower pots, and an old yellow surfboard.

3
00:00:20.935 --> 00:00:25.379
"Caroline!" Dad ran outside, sounding worried.

4
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:29.702
"You're late again . . . why didn't you text me?"

5
00:00:29.703 --> 00:00:39.008
Caroline sighed. "Relax, Dad, I was just talking to kids from jazz band."

6
00:00:39.009 --> 00:00:43.723
"Oh! Do they live in Luna Bay, and are they. . . ?"

7
00:00:43.724 --> 00:00:48.413
"Ugh, here we go again!" Caroline thought, annoyed.

8
00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:55.755
Ever since she'd started middle school, Dad had been questioning her about every aspect of her life.

9
00:00:55.756 --> 00:01:00.006
He asked about her friends, her plans, her—

10
00:01:00.007 --> 00:01:02.987
"Hey!" Dad's face lit up.

11
00:01:02.988 --> 00:01:06.653
"Let's invite your friends to eat tacos with us on Tuesday!

12
00:01:06.654 --> 00:01:08.489
Do they like tacos?"

13
00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.201
"No!" Caroline said.

14
00:01:11.202 --> 00:01:18.609
"I mean, maybe they like tacos, but I'm not inviting Austin and Betsy over."

15
00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.843
"Why not?"

16
00:01:20.844 --> 00:01:24.675
"Because you'll interrogate them!"

17
00:01:24.676 --> 00:01:30.656
"I promise," he started, placing a hand over his heart, "no questions!

18
00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:34.081
I won't even ask them to pass the hot sauce!"

19
00:01:34.082 --> 00:01:43.190
"Then you'll find another way to humiliate me . . . like singing really old songs! So no, absolutely not!"

20
00:01:43.191 --> 00:01:47.942
"Okay," Dad mumbled with hurt in his voice.

21
00:01:47.943 --> 00:01:55.802
The following week Caroline stayed after school every day for jazz band, remembering to text Dad.

22
00:01:55.803 --> 00:02:00.703
But on Wednesday, when she biked home with Austin, she forgot.

23
00:02:00.704 --> 00:02:04.137
Dad was annoyed but let it go.

24
00:02:04.138 --> 00:02:09.830
On Friday, after rehearsal ran late, Caroline pulled out her phone and panicked.

25
00:02:09.831 --> 00:02:12.215
Her battery was dead!

26
00:02:12.216 --> 00:02:20.059
She looked around, hoping to borrow a phone from her friends, but Betsy and Austin had already left.

27
00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:28.104
Finally she hopped on her bike and breathlessly pedaled home, where she explained what happened.

28
00:02:28.105 --> 00:02:32.239
"That's not an excuse!" Dad snapped.

29
00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.501
"You've been late multiple times without informing me, so from now on, I'm picking you up from rehearsal."

30
00:02:38.502 --> 00:02:43.410
"That's totally ridiculous—I'm not in kindergarten!"

31
00:02:43.411 --> 00:02:48.711
Caroline persisted and kept arguing, but Dad wouldn't budge.

32
00:02:48.712 --> 00:02:56.569
On Saturday Dad gave Caroline permission to go to Betsy's house before he mysteriously left.

33
00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:01.532
After last night's argument, she was still feeling angry at him.

34
00:03:01.533 --> 00:03:05.392
Austin was already at Betsy's house when she arrived.

35
00:03:05.393 --> 00:03:09.662
"Let's go down to Luna Beach," he said.

36
00:03:09.663 --> 00:03:12.919
A few minutes later, they reached the ocean.

37
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:19.797
The blue water glistened in the sunlight, and tall waves curled toward the shore.

38
00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:28.959
Surfers in wet suits were out in the water, struggling to stand on their boards while an instructor bellowed tips.

39
00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:34.430
"Whoa!" Austin said as a huge wave tossed a man off his board.

40
00:03:34.431 --> 00:03:37.913
"That dude had a spectacular wipeout!"

41
00:03:37.914 --> 00:03:41.815
Caroline watched the surfer climb back on his yellow board.

42
00:03:41.816 --> 00:03:45.382
As he started paddling, she gasped.

43
00:03:45.383 --> 00:03:48.177
"That's my father!"

44
00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:53.553
Betsy laughed. "Your dad takes surfing lessons?"

45
00:03:53.554 --> 00:04:03.356
"Apparently!" Caroline stiffened, waiting for her friends to poke fun at her dad, but instead they sounded impressed.

46
00:04:03.357 --> 00:04:05.865
"Awesome," Austin said.

47
00:04:05.866 --> 00:04:09.539
"He's got guts!" Betsy said.

48
00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.662
Caroline shook her head, still unable to comprehend what she was seeing.

49
00:04:14.663 --> 00:04:19.395
"Do you guys mind if we get out of here?"

50
00:04:19.396 --> 00:04:23.155
That night at dinner, the air still felt tense.

51
00:04:23.156 --> 00:04:27.512
Caroline stayed quiet as Dad passed the potatoes.

52
00:04:27.513 --> 00:04:30.382
"How was your afternoon?"

53
00:04:30.383 --> 00:04:33.319
Caroline pushed some peas around.

54
00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:39.482
"Betsy lives near the ocean, so we walked to Luna Beach, and . . ."

55
00:04:39.483 --> 00:04:47.277
She glanced up, inhaling sharply before blurting out, "We watched some surfers and I saw you!"

56
00:04:47.278 --> 00:04:50.028
Dad nearly dropped his fork.

57
00:04:50.029 --> 00:04:54.923
"Why didn't you tell me about the surfing lessons?"

58
00:04:54.924 --> 00:05:00.174
He hung his head. "It sounds dumb, but I was too embarrassed.

59
00:05:00.175 --> 00:05:06.088
I wanted to feel confident that I could actually surf first." He sighed.

60
00:05:06.089 --> 00:05:10.259
"I didn't want to talk about it until I was ready."

61
00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.568
Caroline nodded slowly.

62
00:05:12.569 --> 00:05:17.753
"I get it because sometimes I don't feel like talking about stuff either.

63
00:05:17.754 --> 00:05:19.521
But you keep asking—"

64
00:05:19.522 --> 00:05:22.398
"Too many questions," Dad jumped in.

65
00:05:22.399 --> 00:05:26.851
"I've been thinking . . . You can ride your bike home from rehearsal.

66
00:05:26.852 --> 00:05:32.459
And from now on, I'll try to give you some space when you don't feel like talking."

67
00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.727
He cast a hopeful look at her.

68
00:05:34.728 --> 00:05:38.400
"It might help if I could meet your new friends."

69
00:05:38.401 --> 00:05:42.510
"Well, guess what—they want to meet you too."

70
00:05:42.511 --> 00:05:46.549
"Huh?" This time Dad did drop his fork.

71
00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.279
Caroline grinned.

72
00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:56.559
"They think it's cool you're a surfer, so I invited them over for dinner on Tuesday!"

